// PiccoloConsole.dll pelex.cpp (0x1001be10-0x1001cba9): the scanner of the
// syntax colouring of the editor, generated by flex 2.4 from the scanner
// description of the Piccolo compiler (the same patterns) with actions that
// report every token's kind and length to the line being coloured.
//
// The rules, in order (found by simulating the DFA of the tables):
//   1 [ \t\r]+   2 \n   3 "/*" (a comment, on to its end or the end of the line)
//   4 "//" (a comment to the end of the line)   5 hexadecimal   6 octal
//   7 decimal   8 float   9 identifier, keyword or global symbol
//   10-54 operators   55 \" (a string)   56 ' (a character)
//   57-61 @ # $ ` \ (illegal characters)   62 default rule
// The start conditions STRING, CHAR, CHAREND and ESCAPE of the compiler's
// scanner are declared but have no rules here.
//
// The kinds of tokens (the colours of MfPeTextLine): 1 keyword, 2 identifier,
// 3 string or character, 4 number, 6 comment, 7 global symbol.
